courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon successfully completing this course, students will be able to:
a) Critical reasoning with respect to music and its discourses;
b) Standard research tools, library resources and online databases;
c) Proposing and developing appropriate level research projects;
d) Formal writing standards (bibliographic style, citations, etc.).

Upon successfully completing this course, students will be able:
a) To formulate and tackle relevant research/artistic questions;
b) To acquire and consolidate research and academic/creative writing skills;
c) To cultivate critical thinking/artistic expressivity.

Upon successfully completing this course, students will:
a) Be familiar with the techniques in sound production and sound synthesis control;
b) Be able to apply the techniques learnt to compose or arrange music;
c) Show an appropriate level of computer programming in writing music software for different needs;
d) Be able to analyze, criticize and compare different stylistic electronic music;
e) Be able to writing music for interactive multi media music.

Upon successfully completing this course, students will have:
a) Gained an understanding of major theories and models of ethnomusicology;
b) Acquired knowledge of key historical issues that contributed to the development of ethnomusicology;
c) Developed research writing and academic presentation skills;
d) Developed critical thinking and foundational research methods in the field of ethnomusicology.

Upon successfully completing this course, students will have:
a) Gained an understanding of selected topics in Chinese music;
b) Acquired broad knowledge of issues in the study of Chinese music;
c) Developed research writing and academic presentation skills;
d) Developed critical thinking and foundational research methods in Chinese music studies.

