c) Developed research writing and academic presentation skills;
d) Developed critical thinking and foundational research methods in Chinese music studies.

Upon successfully completing this course, students will be able to:
a) Understand and engage in the major theoretical, methodological, and analytical debates pertinent to the discipline of Ethnomusicology and related academic fields;
b) Sharpen analysis skills relevant to selected dimensions of world music traditions;
c) Gain deeper familiarity of a variety of musical and performance styles from outside of China and the West;
d) Pursue original research through the application of interdisciplinary and innovative approaches.

