Upon completion of the course, students will be able to:
a) Identify and critique the monuments of Renaissance and Baroque music;
b) Begin to place them in their various contexts, whether cultural, political, economic, et al.;
c) Critique the vast primary source writings about Renaissance and Baroque music, testing the boundaries between theory and practice;
d) Employ the library scientific skills requisite for engaging this vast repertoire.

